# Targets to delete from the destination on apply.
#
# Dropping a file from the source only makes chezmoi stop managing it; the copy
# already written to a machine stays exactly where it is. That is fine for most
# retired files and not fine for this one, so it is listed here explicitly.

# 10-autowatch.zsh hooked chpwd to `source` and then `eval` a .watchrc from
# whatever directory had just been entered, giving any cloned repository under
# ~/repositories arbitrary code execution on cd. Removed in favour of direnv,
# which gates the same behaviour behind `direnv allow`. Leaving the orphaned
# copy in place would keep it armed on every machine that ever applied it,
# since ~/.config/zsh/*.zsh is glob-sourced by .zshrc and would still pick it
# up. Safe to prune from this file once every machine has applied once.
.config/zsh/10-autowatch.zsh

# ~/.firefox-policies.json was only ever a staging copy: the 170-firefox-policies
# scripts read it and wrote it out to wherever that host's Firefox actually
# looks for policies.json. The document now lives in
# .chezmoitemplates/firefox-policies.json and is emitted inline by those
# scripts, so nothing reads this path any more -- but every machine that
# applied before the move still has it sitting in $HOME. Safe to prune from
# this file once every machine has applied once.
.firefox-policies.json
